# Added 2026-08-06 (handoff Sec 1.3): [NeIII] 3869,3968 (finishes the
# previously-commented-out scaffolding in EMSpectrum.spectrum()), [OIII]
# 4363 (auroral, direct-Te diagnostic), [NII] 5755 (auroral), [SII]
# 4068,4076 (auroral doublet). Vacuum wavelengths are best-available
# estimates from standard nebular line-list conventions (consistent with
# common SDSS-pipeline vacuum values) -- flagged for a final cross-check
# against a definitive source (e.g. NIST ASD, or whatever "impro" source
# the rest of this file's wavelengths came from) before treating them as
# exact. The 'ratio' column here is the usual dummy placeholder -- actual
# ratios (both narrow and broad-AGN-like) are drawn/set in
# EMSpectrum.spectrum(), same as [OI]/[SIII]/[ArIII]/MgII. Rows are only
# present in EMSpectrum.line when include_new_lines=True was passed to
# __init__ (removed otherwise, mirroring the include_mgii pattern), so
# default (opt-out) behavior for every existing caller is unaffected.
[NeIII]_3869 3869.86  1.0
[NeIII]_3968 3968.59  1.0
[OIII]_4363  4364.44  1.0
[NII]_5755   5756.24  1.0
[SII]_4068   4069.75  1.0
[SII]_4076   4077.50  1.0
